# homelab-node-exporter: extra node_exporter flags for THIS host.
#
# Read by the package's systemd drop-in (EnvironmentFile). Edit, then
# `systemctl restart prometheus-node-exporter`. Reinstalling keeps this file.
#
# Default: the zfs and systemd collectors are OFF. Measured 2026-11-09
# (post-cutover #18) on a 56-host fleet holding 433k series:
#  * zfs -- inside an LXC container /proc/spl/kstat/zfs is the HYPERVISOR's
#    ZFS, so all 46 containers reported pve2's ~150 datasets identically:
#    46 copies of the same 4,459 series, 205k series, 47% of everything.
#    The VMs expose nothing there. A host with ZFS of its own can drop
#    --no-collector.zfs here.
#  * systemd -- node_systemd_unit_state is every unit x 5 states, ~800
#    series per host, 45k fleet-wide (10%), and nothing reads it: the
#    dashboards, alert rules and myaccount's Metrics tab use none of it, and
#    homelab-agent's homelab_service_up already covers the services that
#    matter.
HOMELAB_COLLECTOR_ARGS="--no-collector.zfs --no-collector.systemd"
